<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Petrify (240)</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>petrify &lt;player or monster&gt;
</pre>
<p>Turns someone to stone by your gaze: a punishment, or a scene. The room 
sees you gaze into their eyes, and they turn to stone.
</p><p><b>A player</b> is taken out of play: a statue of them stands where they 
were, and they are held in a room apart until you petrify them again. 
Then they return to flesh where the statue stands (or where they were, if 
the statue is gone). A player who is dead at the moment can't be 
petrified; wait until they are back.
</p><p><b>A monster</b> is replaced by a statue, for good.
</p><p>It works on anyone in the game of a lower level than yours, but not on 
things. It is logged. Not to be confused with the druids' petrify spell 
(see <a cmd='#'>Help Petrify</a>).
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Freeze</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Petrify</a>
</pre>




</div>